# What `cargo fuzz` writes into this directory. Local rather than a set of
# entries in the root `.gitignore`, because the root file is W00's and because
# every path here is meaningful only next to this manifest.
target/
corpus/
artifacts/
coverage/

# The fuzz package is its own workspace (see Cargo.toml), so it resolves its own
# lockfile. Not committed: it is a nightly-only developer tool that no CI job
# builds, `cargo deny` reads the workspace lockfile and never this one, and a
# second lockfile that nothing checks is a supply-chain claim nobody is making.
# What a fuzzing run has to be reproducible against is the corpus and the target,
# and the corpus is the artifact worth keeping.
Cargo.lock
